From 332959beae3cfdada4ed363eb5674b9ec801aa43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:54:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] luma: one placement rule for every surface opened from
 the shelf

Quick Options, the clock, dock tooltips, dock menus, window previews and the
Well's popover and menus each measured their distance from something
different: the status button plus the popover's beak (14px), the dock icon
(tooltips), the island with a Math.max against the theme gap, or a local
8 * scale. They did not line up, and a height-limited menu such as a Well
item's opened 31px above its island.

There is now one rule and one constant. SHELF_SURFACE_GAP (8, logical) sits
with the other shelf metrics in shelfMetrics.js, and shelfSurfacePlacement()
puts a surface that far beyond the desktop-facing edge of the painted island
holding the control that opened it, centred on that control; when centring
would cross the 14px inset it aligns with the island's edge instead.
lumaShelfSurface.js finds the island (the 0062 parent walk, generalised to
every island, or the whole shelf when it paints one connected surface) and is
the only way a surface is placed:

- BoxPointer menus opened from an island are marked luma-shelf-surface, have
  no beak, and are placed from the size they are allocated, replacing the
  0062 override and its Math.max(gap, 8 * scale).
- Dock tooltips are placed by the rule and follow their final size; the
  -y-offset: 16px rule is gone.
- Window previews use the shared rule and constants instead of 8 * scale.
- The -boxpointer-gap: 8px rule for the Well and shelf menus is gone.

Dropping this patch restores each surface's previous placement.
